WEBVTT

00:00:11.949 --> 00:00:13.229
Why a card is declined.

00:00:15.091 --> 00:00:16.030
It starts at the checkout:

00:00:16.286 --> 00:00:19.059
a card number, a date, a security code,

00:00:19.443 --> 00:00:20.143
and Place order.

00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:22.216
Most of the time the answer is yes.

00:00:22.771 --> 00:00:23.582
Sometimes it is no.

00:00:25.063 --> 00:00:26.471
A decline is the bank's answer.

00:00:27.196 --> 00:00:28.647
The payment reaches the card's bank,

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:30.439
and the bank sends back no,

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:31.480
with a short reason.

00:00:32.145 --> 00:00:33.852
That reason decides what works next.

00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:39.089
Four reasons come up again and again.

00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:40.411
Not enough funds:

00:00:40.966 --> 00:00:42.715
the account cannot cover the charge today.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:43.970
Do not honor:

00:00:44.422 --> 00:00:46.043
the bank says no and gives no reason.

00:00:46.598 --> 00:00:47.298
A dead card:

00:00:47.537 --> 00:00:49.201
lost, stolen or closed.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:50.812
And the bank's own fraud rule,

00:00:51.196 --> 00:00:52.305
which stopped this one charge.

00:00:55.831 --> 00:00:56.531
What works next?

00:00:57.026 --> 00:00:59.543
On a rebill, trying the same card again

00:00:59.671 --> 00:01:00.371
rarely does:

00:01:00.695 --> 00:01:01.762
the bank gives the same answer.

00:01:02.231 --> 00:01:03.852
A different card usually gets a yes.

00:01:05.424 --> 00:01:07.856
After not enough funds, the same card pays

00:01:07.941 --> 00:01:09.051
about one time in seven;

00:01:09.477 --> 00:01:11.355
a different card, three times in four.

00:01:11.952 --> 00:01:14.256
After a dead card, the same card pays

00:01:14.299 --> 00:01:15.280
one time in seventy;

00:01:15.451 --> 00:01:17.584
a different card, four times in five.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:21.866
When the customer is there,

00:01:22.378 --> 00:01:23.616
most declines get fixed.

00:01:24.128 --> 00:01:26.432
On the web, about two in three end

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.522
paid, and nearly half within the hour.

00:01:29.034 --> 00:01:30.400
A rebill has nobody there:

00:01:30.912 --> 00:01:33.130
three in four are not recovered within a month.

00:01:36.389 --> 00:01:37.285
Some reasons mislead.

00:01:37.754 --> 00:01:39.290
Pick up card sounds like a card to

00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:40.033
take away;

00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:41.935
one version of it is a bank fraud

00:01:42.021 --> 00:01:44.324
rule that clears, and the same card pays

00:01:44.453 --> 00:01:45.989
again about one time in four.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.078
And a reply that reads like a spending

00:01:48.249 --> 00:01:50.510
limit can mean the bank wants the identity check.

00:01:53.948 --> 00:01:55.996
So today, in the United States and Canada,

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.897
every declined rebill is sorted by its reason.

00:01:59.751 --> 00:02:00.451
Retry:

00:02:00.604 --> 00:02:01.884
tried again after three days.

00:02:02.439 --> 00:02:03.139
Update the card:

00:02:03.335 --> 00:02:04.615
only a new card will work.

00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:05.869
Stop:

00:02:05.895 --> 00:02:06.620
never tried again.

00:02:07.004 --> 00:02:08.369
About half go to the retry.

00:02:10.495 --> 00:02:11.647
Why a card is declined:

00:02:12.287 --> 00:02:13.140
the bank gives a reason,

00:02:13.652 --> 00:02:14.932
the reason picks the next step,

00:02:15.231 --> 00:02:17.764
and a different card beats the same card.

